  "summary": "The Humboldt County Sheriff's Office confirms that seven of its nine Flock ALPR cameras are out of service due to vandalism, with only two still operational. A Redheaded Blackbelt site visit found poles downed or stripped of camera units at multiple mapped locations, and HCSO says an investigation is underway.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The Humboldt County Sheriff's Office says seven of its Flock license plate reader cameras are down due to vandalism, and only two are still in service.",
      "paragraph_idx": 2
    },
    {
      "quote": "Two cameras are in service. The rest\u2026are all down due to vandalism.",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "The California Highway Patrol told Redheaded Blackbelt it has never had Flock cameras in Humboldt County.",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
